    "raw": "Parent: d46c7c66 (Groom musicology tags).\n\n## Rule (amended)\nEvery directory that is an album (directly contains audio) is a scan/rename unit\n**regardless of hierarchy depth** \u2014 top-level under `files/` or nested under a\nbox/container.\n\n## Homogeneous multi-disc (Woodstock / Caf\u00e9 CD1\u2026)\nExample: `\u2026/The Woodstock & Flower Power Generation (10 Disc's) by Art&Music`\n\u2192 `Vol. 01` \u2026 `Vol. 10`.\n\n1. **Individually:** musicscan each disc/vol child.\n2. **As a collection:** musicscan the parent box, then write parent\n   `.meta.combined.json` as provider tags \u222a set-union of children\u2019s combined tags.\n\n## Heterogeneous boxes (Doors Infinite)\nExample: `\u2026/Doors - Infinite/` with child dirs that are **distinct albums**\n(`The Doors - 1967 - Strange Days [\u2026]`, \u2026).\n\n1. musicscan / rename **each child album** (same rules as top-level albums).\n2. **No** parent musicscan / parent union (avoids polluting the box with a\n   fake single-album identity).\n\n`Hi-Res Masters - 2000s` = flat compilation (one unit), not nested albums.\n\n## Empirics\nWoodstock vols: sidecars present, providers unmatched; dual treatment still right.\nDoors Infinite: postingest discovers 6 audio children and skips parent union\n(verified dry-run). Child dirnames still need correct-flac-names (The-strip,\nyear/edition denoise) \u2014 previously deferred; **now in scope**.\n\n## Also in scope (amend)\nNested `correct-flac-names` via `shadup mv` for album dirs at any depth\n(Doors Infinite children and similar boxes).\n\n## Out of scope\nfix-junk-nested-albums.sh physical moves (separate).\n\n## Musicology fixpoint (cursor)\nProviders = working set (typically musicbrainz, discogs, lastfm); n = |providers|.\nBudget: **max 2n** provider lookups per album.\n\n1. **Round 1 (\u2264 n):** query each provider from dirname guesses; on hit, **lock** that\n   provider with its returned metadata.\n2. **Round 2 (\u2264 n remaining):** for each still-missed provider, retry using each\n   locked provider\u2019s artist/album metadata as the query (in turn) until hit or\n   budget exhausted.\n3. **Johan write:** if a single metadata set produces hits for **all** providers,\n   write that artist/album into `.meta.johan.json` (curated override)."
  },
